<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saragurs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saragurs were a nomadic people who appeared in the steppes north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> around 463, according to the Byzantine historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/priscus">Priscus</a>. Driven west by the Sabirs, they displaced the Akatziri, sent envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and raided Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> through the Caucasus. They are generally counted among the early Oghur peoples related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a>.</p></div>
